    <l n="1" type="heading" level="2" para="true">Cap. X. De subjecto.</l>
    <l n="2" para="true">ARgumentum modo quodam cõ-</l>
    <l n="3">sentaneũ succedit:ut subjectũ &amp;</l>
    <l n="4">adjunctum. Subjectum eft, cui aliquid</l>
    <l n="5">adjungitur. Anima, eft subjectum scien-</l>
    <l n="6">tiæ,ignorantiæ,virtutis, vitii: Corpus,sa-</l>
    <l n="7">nitatis, morbi,roboris,infirmitatis,pul-</l>
    <l n="8">chritudinis,deformitatis.Homo,subje-</l>
    <l n="9">ctum eft divitiarum,paupertatis,hono-</l>
    <l n="10">ris,infamiæ,veftitus,comitatus.Locus,</l>
    <l n="11">eft spatium rei locatæ:Sic philosophi di-</l>
    <l n="12">vinis entib9, licet parte &amp; magnitudine</l>
    <l n="13">carentibus, attribuūt locũ: sic Geome-</l>
    <l n="14">træ, locum lociq; differentias in rebus</l>
    <l n="15">Geometricis:sic Physici etiam multó di-</l>
    <l n="16">ligentiús,in rebus physicis considerant,</l>
    <l n="17">in mundo,in elementis simplicibus, in</l>
